valent one good affordable option we  recommend is TCL's 55 p 605 you can  typically find it online for around 600  bucks and it comes with dolby vision HDR  if you want to go the extra mile you  could opt to get a 4k HDR oled TV which  will offer true  since they don't use traditional LEDs  and instead up to use individually  backlit pixels however while OLED panels  are certainly nice they generally cost a  lot more and are thus relegated in the  nice-to-haves category but when it comes  to HDR the slight premium you might pay  is worth it considering it will be  another prominent display standard  moving forward in the end if you're  gonna spend hundreds of dollars to  purchase a nice 4k TV it might as well  make sure it's more future proof by  ensuring it supports HDR for more  information on how HDR FX games make  sure to check out our pc graphics  settings explainer video thanks for  watching
 

